 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The regular past",
   "texto": [
    "The past is used to count finished facts: **Jeg jobbet i går** («I worked yesterday.»). Many verbs form the past with **-et** or **-te**: jobbe → jobbet, kjøpe → kjøpte.",
    "The verbal form does not change according to the person: **jeg jobbet**, **hun jobbet**. In questions of yes or no, the verb goes before the subject: **Jobbet du i går?**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The time at first",
   "texto": [
    "If an expression of time goes to the beginning, the conjugated verb is second: **I går jobbet jeg hjemme**. In Spanish, «I worked yesterday.» is usually maintained; in Norwegian the subject passes after the verb."
   ]
  },
